8. CRITICAL FEATURE: NON-CIRCUMVENTION & ANTI-BYPASS PROTECTION

This feature is extremely important to Aabest Services' business interests.

The project opportunity is being coordinated through an intermediary. The registration process must clearly establish the relationship between the applicant, the coordinating party and the project opportunity.

The supplied Truck Owner & Contractor Agreement contains a specific Non-Circumvention clause.

It states that the Truck Owner acknowledges that the project opportunity was facilitated exclusively through Sleek Investment Consult and agrees not to bypass the Consultant by directly negotiating with project parties without prior written consent.

Use the actual agreement as the source for the legal wording.

IMPORTANT: Do not silently substitute Aabest Services for Sleek Investment Consult in the legal agreement. The contracting party and Aabest Services' role must be confirmed before any agreement is presented as legally binding.

8.1 Mandatory Non-Circumvention Agreement

Before final submission, display a dedicated agreement acceptance page.

Use a professional legal document presentation layout.

The agreement should establish:

The applicant acknowledges the introduction to the project through the designated coordinating party.

The applicant agrees not to circumvent or bypass the designated Consultant or authorized project coordinator.

The applicant must not use project contacts, introductions, information or opportunities obtained through the registration process to negotiate directly with project parties in a manner that excludes the designated Consultant.

All project-related negotiations, commercial discussions and operational arrangements arising from this introduction must follow the authorized coordination process.

The applicant must not introduce associated companies, agents, representatives or third parties as a means of circumventing the agreed arrangement.

Any exception must receive prior written authorization from the designated Consultant.

The applicant acknowledges that submission of registration details does not automatically guarantee approval, deployment or a contract.

The above must be treated as proposed website agreement content requiring legal review and approval. Do not present it as a verbatim reproduction of the supplied agreement.

8.2 Applicant Agreement Acceptance

Require the applicant to:

Read the agreement.

Scroll through the entire agreement.

Tick a mandatory acceptance checkbox.

Enter their full legal name.

Select their capacity (Truck Owner, Enterprise Representative or Authorized Representative).

Provide their electronic signature by typing their full legal name.

Enter the date.

Confirm that they understand the non-circumvention obligation.

The checkbox must be unchecked by default.

Do not allow the demonstration form to proceed without the required acknowledgement.

8.3 Individual Driver Declaration

